Every module checks the product version before its first request, including
unchanged and read-only runs.

An untested product series produces one warning and the module proceeds.
Operations known to fail on a particular product build fail before they write.



## Usage<a id="usage"></a>

Each section below covers one administration task: what its modules manage and
refuse, what you prepare. It ends with an example task list and the names of its
modules;
`ansible-doc {{ namespace }}.{{ collection_name }}.<module>`
shows a module's options, return values and own rules. The examples are tasks of
this play, run on the control node against an inventory host that defines the
endpoint's variables:

```yaml
---
- name: "Configure {{ product | default('Example Product') }}"
  hosts: "product_api"
  connection: "local"
  gather_facts: false
  become: false
  module_defaults:
    group/{{ namespace }}.{{ collection_name }}.api:
      url: "{% raw %}{{ product_url }}{% endraw %}"
      api_key: "{% raw %}{{ product_api_key }}{% endraw %}"
      api_secret: "{% raw %}{{ product_api_secret }}{% endraw %}"
  tasks: # the tasks of the section
```

